      "id": "6656566",
      "title": "Introduction & Why Pipes are Useful",
      "lectureOrder": 565,
      "videoOrder": 518,
      "sourceHash": "5e29a152288ccc112d32e1be7bca5776bca71df9c1580f73be37ef27b40b989e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.67,
          "end": 4.62,
          "en": "-: Welcome to a new core section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.62,
          "end": 8.43,
          "en": "This core section is about Pipes, and let's start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.43,
          "end": 12.69,
          "en": "with the most important question first, what are Pipes?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.69,
          "end": 16.59,
          "en": "Pipes are a feature built into Angler two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.59,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "which basically allows you to transform output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 21.09,
          "en": "in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.09,
          "end": 23.37,
          "en": "This is the main purpose of a pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.37,
          "end": 25.83,
          "en": "It transforms some output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.83,
          "end": 28.036,
          "en": "Now, there are pipes for different types of output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.036,
          "end": 32.64,
          "en": "and also for synchronous and asynchronous data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.64,
          "end": 34.86,
          "en": "We will have a look at this throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.86,
          "end": 37.44,
          "en": "The general theme is always the same, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.44,
          "end": 39.84,
          "en": "A basic example would be the following.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.84,
          "end": 43.35,
          "en": "You have a username, that's a property in your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.35,
          "end": 47.13,
          "en": "For example, here, it holds a string, Max.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.13,
          "end": 49.83,
          "en": "Now you want your output, that username in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.83,
          "end": 53.34,
          "en": "And for this, you probably use string interpolation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.34,
          "end": 55.41,
          "en": "as you learn it throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.41,
          "end": 59.52,
          "en": "Now, that's all right, but then you decide it would be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.52,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "if the output, which is Max, if you do it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 68.4,
          "en": "would be all upper case, but only when you output it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.4,
          "end": 72.06,
          "en": "So, you don't wanna change the property itself to uppercase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.06,
          "end": 75.18,
          "en": "because imagine you use that for all your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 79.17,
          "en": "and it should still be well, as you assigned it up there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.17,
          "end": 81.84,
          "en": "but you want to transform the way it is displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.84,
          "end": 84.45,
          "en": "once you render it to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.45,
          "end": 86.91,
          "en": "Now, for this, you could use a pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.91,
          "end": 89.03999999999999,
          "en": "Namely the uppercase pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.03999999999999,
          "end": 91.32,
          "en": "This actually would be a built-in pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.32,
          "end": 95.07,
          "en": "and we will have a look at the built-in pipes in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.07,
          "end": 98.00999999999999,
          "en": "Now, with that built-in pipe in use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 102.45,
          "en": "you would now see Max, all uppercase being printed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.45,
          "end": 105.72,
          "en": "to the screen because this is what this pipe does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.72,
          "end": 107.97,
          "en": "It transforms the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.97,
          "end": 112.02000000000001,
          "en": "Now, that is the main purpose of pipes, transforming values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.02000000000001,
          "end": 114.36,
          "en": "Let's dive into them a bit more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.36,
          "end": 116.61,
          "en": "Let's view some of the built-in pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.61,
          "end": 118.77000000000001,
          "en": "and then let's also build our own pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.77000000000001,
          "end": 119.60300000000001,
          "en": "Let's go.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
